:: Carter Hero's Weakness Part 1 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 10>>
<<set $HangOutNeed to {
    Energy: 100,
    Fun: 20,
    Comfort: 20,
}>>
Your knocking on the door is met with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> answering it a few moments later. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span>!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says happily, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I knew you’d come over. Couldn't resist the urge to be a hero, eh?”</span> He smirks as you roll your eyes, walking inside. As <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> said, the house is dead quiet, <span style="color:Yellow">and you find it surprising that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s parents would actually leave him home alone.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m very responsible! They leave me home alone a bunch!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> replies, sounding slightly offensive, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Plus, they didn’t really have a choice, so-”</span> He shrugs. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
                },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
        ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> leads you into his bedroom, where his TV is on playing a cartoon and a half-eaten bag of chips sits beside his beanbag. He quickly cleans up before telling you to hold on a second as he slips under his bed to grab something. <span style="color:Pink">You watch his butt sway about as he searches, his underwear slightly poking out of his shorts as he does so. You smile at the view until he crawls back out holding a small box.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s in here! Check it out, they are so cool!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> opens the box on his bed, spilling out the contents. There are a few random items, a shiny rock or two, an old bottlecap, but the main item is actually pretty surprising. <span style="color:Yellow">A shiny, metal pair of police handcuffs!</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s not a toy either, they’re real! Here, feel it.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> hands them to you and you are a bit surprised by the weight. <span style="color:Pink">They aren’t just plastic toy cuffs, but real metal handcuffs!</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> grabs the key from the pile and unlocks them, allowing you to inspect and confirm just how real they are. <span style="color:Yellow">The obvious question is raised to the surface, why the heck does <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> have a pair of handcuffs!?</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                },
                },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                    Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Haha, they’re dad’s. Or they were. He got some new ones a while back and let me have these ones since I always thought they were cool. He told me to be careful with them, since they’re not a toy, but they are fun to mess around with. Though…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> blushes a little, smiling shyly, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I got stuck a few weeks ago. I know how to use them so you can get them off without them locking, but I messed up and handcuffed myself to my bed.”</span> You snort at his admission, <span style="color:Pink">finding it an obvious result of playing with real handcuffs.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I hardly ever get stuck!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> argues, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And whenever I do, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> normally helps me or I can get myself out after a while. Dad just found me first that day. He took them away, but I’ve been begging for them back since and he gave them back when I promised to be more careful!”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, then, immediately tries to show you how cool they are and how he can use them in his games to pretend to be captured by the villains. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It makes it super realistic!”</span> He explains, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And I know a trick so they don’t actually lock and you can just slip out of them, but they feel like they’re really on and stuff.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> proceeds to show you, cuffing his hands behind his back like some captured hero. <span style="color:Pink">Then, as he tries to show you how he slips out, there is a loud click before <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s eyes suddenly go wide.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                    Eyes: "Tired",
                },
                },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Blush: 2,
                    Arms: "Bound",
                },
            },
        ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ummm, hold on-! I got-!”</span> <span style="color:Pink"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> struggles back and forth a little as it becomes very clear that, whether due to lack of practice or handcuffs really not being meant to be played with, that he has actually handcuffed his hands behind his back.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“So… uhh…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> turns to you with a nervous smile, blushing bright pink, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I- I may have… messed up when trying to… Could- could you use the key and unlock me? Please?”</span> <span style="color:Pink">You can’t help but break out laughing, much to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s embarrassment, asking what he would have done if you didn’t come over. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> would have been stuck like that until his parents got home.</span> <br>
<br>

